evention at Self-Checkout One of the bigger retail developments of the last decade is the appearance of self-checkout lines at major retailers. Eliminating the cashier (scanning each item, interacting with customers, observing behavior) presents an obvious barrier to loss prevention efforts. Target approached this problem by leaning hard into one of the anti-shoplifting tactics above:","ok":true,"op":"document"},"time":6},"model_calls":19,"document_judgments":11,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
