{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-153051","model_call":67,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1305"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1305"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1015268761#15_2109808748","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1305","rank":3,"snippet":"v2.1_doc_40_1015268761#15_2109808748\" , \"end_char\": 8873.000000 , \"headings\": \"10 Ways to Stop Shoplifting in Your Retail Store 10 Ways to Stop Shoplifting in Your Retail Store 10 effective ways to prevent shoplifting in your retail store: 1. Keep your store organized and tidy 2. Be aware of common <cover>shoplifting tactics 3. Optimize your store’s layout 4. Install security cameras 5. Add mirrors to your store 6. Use customer service as prevention 7. Use signage to deter thieves 8. Train your employees 9. Use retail inventory management tools 10. Identify at-risk items Keep shoplifters at bay with these 10 tips \" , \"segment\": \"10. Identify at-risk items Your average shoplifter won’t target </cover>items such as expensive jewelry or large electronics, instead targeting small, easily swipeable products that are easy to conceal. Use inventory management tools to identify your most expensive inventory, and work out a plan to protect these items. This can involve placing items in lockable cabinets, placing items close to the counter, or placing them in a highly trafficked area of the store that’s ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2021688056#1_3321145933","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_2021688056#0_3321144158","rank":2,"relevance":3}]},"time":7},"model_calls":67,"document_judgments":27,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
