{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-153051","model_call":90,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1324"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1324"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_280206102#6_686414962","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1324","rank":2,"snippet":"store SEE ALSO: Costco employees explain why they don't buy produce there \" , \"segment\": \"\\\"I worked at Target in the early nineties and it was insane then,\\\" another Reddit user added. \\\" Twenty years later and I wouldn't be surprised if they weigh me as I enter and as I leave to determine if I'm shoplifting.\\\" One Target employee told Business Insider that the surveillance system doesn't ensure that all shoplifters get busted immediately, however. \\\"Stores will often let <cover>shoplifters go until they steal an amount that will be counted as a felony — sending them straight to jail,\" the Target employee told Business Insider. </cover>Be nice to employees — it might pay off. AP Photo/Damian Dovarganes Sometimes, it pays to be nice. Business Insider's Kate Taylor previously reported on a viral blog started by Target employee Tom Grennell. He wrote about working during a special sale when his Target store was giving out a 10% discount on all purchases. The store had mailed out a coupon, but if customers forgot their copies, they could ask for another coupon. \"I have a coupon to scan if anyone asks for it.\" ,","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_280206102#6_686414962","rank":2,"relevance":2}]},"time":1},"model_calls":90,"document_judgments":39,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
